      "side": 1,
      "message": "Added `SetFrom` trait, it makes it easier to return single values, which is a common use case.\n\nHowever the macro is still necessary. In earlier versions of this patch I had methods in `SmcReturn` for setting multiple arguments. It had an an impact on the performance, because the caller had to shuffle around/save the registers to be able to make the function call.\n\nThe only way set multiple arguments in `SmcReturn` efficiently is to expose the internal `args` structure to the caller as a reference to an array and write the values directly into that.\n\nWhen exposing the `args` via `mark_used()`, there\u0027s a risk of the caller not setting all items, so I made this macro to keep this consistent.",
      "parentUuid": "72d93099_11e18a19",
